flowchart TB
  accTitle: Vertex traffic and platform architecture
  accDescr: Visitors reach the Traefik gateway either directly using Route 53 DNS or through CloudFront for existing websites. HTTPRoutes forward to isolated application services. Rancher Fleet reconciles the desired state; cert-manager and ExternalDNS manage selected certificates and records. Longhorn provides replicated persistent storage and Garage provides S3-compatible buckets.
  Visitor([Visitors]):::person
  subgraph edge["PUBLIC EDGE"]
    DNS["Route 53<br/>health-checked DNS"]:::cloud
    CDN["CloudFront<br/>existing websites"]:::cloud
  end
  subgraph cluster["VERTEX / FOUR RKE2 NODES"]
    GW["Traefik Gateway<br/>TLS + HTTPRoutes"]:::gateway
    Apps["Application namespaces<br/>services + workloads"]:::workload
    Store["Longhorn<br/>replicated volumes"]:::storage
    Garage["Garage<br/>private object buckets"]:::storage
    Fleet["Rancher Fleet<br/>desired-state reconciliation"]:::control
    Cert["cert-manager + ExternalDNS<br/>certificates and selected DNS"]:::control
  end
  Git["Private Git repository<br/>platform + workloads"]:::source
  Visitor --> DNS
  Visitor --> CDN --> GW
  DNS --> GW --> Apps
  Git --> Fleet -.-> Apps
  Cert -.-> GW
  Apps --> Store
  Apps --> Garage --> Store
